  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Deconstructing CSS Selector**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the provided CSS selector string. My focus is on understanding the hierarchy and target of each element within that long chain. I\'m exploring the individual components to see how they relate to the structure of the HTML and what each nth-of-type selector signifies in practical terms.\n\n\n**Analyzing the \"Actions\" Section**\n\nI\'ve homed in on the \"Actions\" section within the header, specifically `div:nth-of-type(3)`. This section houses the theme toggle, profile link, compare link, wishlist link (with badge), and the cart link (with badge). The user\'s directive to \"Redesign this section\" necessitates a meticulous review of its current design and functionality to inform the redesign process. I\'m focusing on the layout and visual presentation of each element.\n\n\n**Envisioning a Redesign**\n\nI\'m now envisioning a complete visual overhaul for the actions section. My goal is a sleek, elegant, and highly usable design with premium aesthetics. Modern tooltips, pills, and refined icons are top of mind, along with smooth glassmorphism and hover effects. Active badges and clean, thoughtful spacing are crucial for usability. I\'ve also pulled the source code for lines 43-78 of the actions section.\n\n\n**Evaluating the Components**\n\nI\'m now closely examining the individual components within the \"Actions\" section, specifically focusing on the compare, wishlist, and cart links, with a look toward redesign. I\'m paying attention to the styling (gray-600, hover:text-orange-600, transition-colors), relative positioning, and the use of icons and text labels. I\'m keen to understand how to keep each part of the action\'s section, while improving the visual presentation. I\'m evaluating how to improve the visual presentation for clarity and user engagement.\n\n\n**Refining the Cart Icon**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the cart icon\'s badge and surrounding elements to enhance visual appeal. I\'m exploring a pulse effect or glowing indicator for the cart badge to draw attention and also integrating modern styling with a sleek card container around the cart action to create a cohesive and premium look. I also intend to improve the icon itself, to make it more professional.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 921212332
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
