    thinking: "**Considering Compare Icon Options**\n\nI\'ve made progress! I\'m now thinking about how to integrate the `useCompare` hook into the `Header.tsx` file to show a compare badge. I\'m also reviewing the icon options available in `lucide-react` for a suitable visual representation of \"compare.\" Currently, I\'m leaning toward either `ArrowLeftRight` or `Scale`.\n\n\n**Designing Header Actions**\n\nI\'m now focused on redesigning the header actions section to use glassmorphic, interactive container buttons for a modern feel. I plan to use Lucide icons consistently, including replacing the compare emoji with `ArrowLeftRight` or `Scale`. Animated badges for Wishlist and Cart items are also in the works. My goal is a visually appealing and functional header.\n\n\n**Refining Header Interactions**\n\nI\'m now implementing the elevated action pill buttons in the header, with options for a solid orange accent or an icon-only button with a glowing badge for cart items. I\'ve added a compare badge that displays when the `compareItems` array has items. I\'m also adding Persian text sub-labels for clarity and responsive visibility. Next, I\'m working on tooltips or glow badges for visual feedback. Finally, I\'m carefully reviewing `Header.tsx` to ensure imports and context usage are correct, specifically lines 1 to 80.\n\n\n**Analyzing Header Element Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the structure of the header\'s action section, specifically examining the `div.flex.items-center.gap-4.md:gap-6` element to confirm its initial properties, especially the structure of `div:nth-of-type(3)` in `Header.tsx` at line 43. I\'m focusing on crafting a beautifully designed actions container, and evaluating the impact of properties like `flex`, `items-center`, `gap-x`, and conditional breakpoints. I will explore applying this analysis to a new container for the actions with the properties `flex`, `items-center`, and `gap-x`, to make sure that the design of the actions container is optimal.\n\n\n**Evaluating Dark Mode Switch**\n\nI\'m now closely examining the dark mode toggle button\'s implementation, particularly the styling and behavior. I\'m focusing on how the hover effects (`hover:text-orange-600`, etc.) and transitions (`transition-all`, `duration-200`) are applied. I\'m assessing the responsiveness of the icon and text to both light and dark modes, including the use of conditional rendering for the `Sun` and `Moon` icons. I also reviewed the use of Persian text, and how to improve the responsiveness.\n\n\n**Refining Compare UI Element**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"Compare\" UI element, specifically its styling and behavior. I\'m taking the styles for the User icon and applying them to the compare link, with `center justify-center sm:px-3 sm:py-1.5 rounded-xl text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200 hover:text-orange-600 dark:hover:text-orange-400 hover:bg-orange-50/80 dark:hover:bg-gray-800/80 transition-all duration-200 border border-transparent hover:border-orange-100 dark:hover:border-gray-700/60`. I\'m also ensuring the Persian text \"\331\205\331\202\330\247\333\214\330\263\331\207 \331\205\330\255\330\265\331\210\331\204\330\247\330\252\" renders correctly and that the link functions as expected. I aim for a consistent look and feel with other header actions.\n\n\n**Implementing Compare Component**\n\nI\'ve been working on the compare component specifically. I am applying styles from the user icon to the compare link, with `rounded-xl text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200 hover:text-orange-600 dark:hover:text-orange-400 hover:bg-orange-50/80 dark:hover:bg-gray-800/80 transition-all duration-200 border border-transparent hover:border-orange-100 dark:hover:border-gray-700/60 hidden sm:flex`. The Persian text renders correctly, and the link works as intended. I\'m focusing on the component\'s transition effects, especially the hover animations and the number badge.\n\n\n**Refining Wishlist Display**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the wishlist component to refine its visual representation. I\'m focusing on the heart icon\'s styling and hover effects, and I\'m ensuring the heart fills correctly when items are in the wishlist. Also, I\'m working to get the badge animation to be visually appealing, and am targeting improved performance.\n\n\n\n**Enhancing Wishlist Interaction**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the wishlist badge animation, refining the `motion.span` element for a smoother, more visually engaging experience. I\'m focusing on the `scale` animation and the overall visual impact of the badge. I\'m also assessing how to improve the performance of the badge, particularly within the context of the header component. I will continue to focus on creating a pleasing user experience.\n\n\n**Optimizing Cart Display**\n\nI\'m now carefully optimizing the cart display, paying particular attention to the visual feedback of the cart count badge. I\'m reviewing the `motion.span` element for performance and visual clarity, including tweaking the `scale` animation and positioning. I\'m focused on achieving a seamless and responsive experience, especially ensuring that the badge and cart icon work together perfectly.\n\n\n"
